BCC_Q({"y": 2024, "n": 2, "part": "A", "topic": "ds", "title": "Digital Image", "answer": 3, "story": "<p>Ana created the following digital image.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A rectangular image with seven parts: top left star, top middle star, top right star, bottom left moon, bottom middle star, bottom right star, and centre star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>She did her work in stages. For the last three stages, she added the\nfollowing parts of the image as shown in order from left to right.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A rectangular image with\none part: the bottom left moon.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/> <img alt=\"A rectangular image with\none part: the centre star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/> <img alt=\"A rectangular image with\none part: the top middle star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>Now Ana has decided to undo some of her work, removing the parts\nadded in the last three stages.<\/p>", "question": "<p>Which of the following options shows the resulting picture?<\/p>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li><img alt=\"A rectangular image with\nfour parts: top left star, top right star, bottom left moon, and bottom\nmiddle star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/><\/li>\n<li><img alt=\"A rectangular image with\nfour parts: top left star, top right star, bottom middle star, and\ncentre star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/><\/li>\n<li><img alt=\"A rectangular image with\nfour parts: top middle star, top right star, bottom left moon, and\nbottom middle star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/><\/li>\n<li><img alt=\"A rectangular image with\nfour parts: top left star, top right star, bottom middle star, and\nbottom left star.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/><\/li>\n<\/ol>", "answerHtml": "<p>(D) <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:30.0%\"/> <\/p>", "explanation": "<p>Undoing the last three stages of Ana’s work in reverse order results\nin the following sequence of pictures.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"header\">\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Part Undone<\/th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Picture Before<\/th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Picture After<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr class=\"even\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100.0%\"/> <\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<p>The final picture above matches Option D.<\/p>", "connections": "<p>This problem simulates a <em>stack data structure<\/em> that uses the\n<em>LIFO<\/em> (Last In First Out) rule: the item that is placed in last\nis the first to be removed. The objects added to the digital image by\nAna can be thought of as elements put, or <em>pushed<\/em>, into a stack.\nWhen parts of the digital image are removed from the picture, these\nelements are removed, or <em>popped<\/em> from the stack.<\/p>\n<p>Stacks are used frequently in computer science. One such usage is\nkeeping track of operations that can be \"undone\", such as edits to a\ndocument, browsing history in a browser, or searching through a maze by\nway of <em>backtracking<\/em> if a dead end is reached.<\/p>", "mc": 1});